{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great","id":1452308,"title":"Revisiting Disciplines - Serpentis (1-3) is really great.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-15T05:29:15-07:00","id":1452308,"title":"Revisiting Disciplines - Serpentis (1-3) is really great.","content":"V20! My old friend! The first TTRPG I ever played!<br /> <br /> After traveling in foreign parts for some time (MTA, D&amp;D 5E, Star Wars FFG), I've started playing VTM again. And having played other systems and learnt a bit more about mechanics in general, I find myself looking at Disciplines quite differently on my return.<br /> <br /> Might as well start with Serpentis!<br /> <br /> 1: This power is better than I remembered! Flavour wise I like the hypnotic gaze vibe, and I like how it acts as a sort of single-person disable. This is a utility power for Vampires, a way to feed safely, a handy way to immobilize a single panicking mortal and give yourself time to think.<br /> <br /> I'll rate this one &quot;If I were a Vampire I would want to have this power.&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;Roll Willpower Difficulty 9 to use this on a Supernatural&quot; feature is interesting, since if you succeed they cannot do anything at all unless you move to harm them in some way, or they are presented with danger. As a result it's a decent hail mary if you're happy to spend a point of Willpower to try and force a success. A sensible GM might put a time limit on this, &quot;he's very strong, you can feel this won't hold him forever&quot;, but it's a neat power.<br /> <br /> Good flavour, good ability, great start.<br /> <br /> 2: Honestly this is a bit too much. V20 and DAV20 both gave this power a lot of love, DAV20 especially. Biting without grappling already makes a Vampire's iconic weapon even stronger. Then add one extra die of damage, and drinking 2 more blood per turn! Just... a really good power.<br /> <br /> The tongue adds a neat new way of attacking people out of reach, and provides a fun and unique way of killing using your snakey vampire. The sensory bonus of flicking and tasting the air is fun too.<br /> <br /> Strong power, very monstrous, main downside is the Masquerade. Both the V20 and DAV20 versions are very strong in combat and provide a lot of utility.<br /> <br /> 3: Arguably the &quot;meta&quot; of dangerous combat in V20 is smacking someone with so much Aggravated that they die in one or two hits. If you want to keep your precious snakey priest safe, Serpentis 3 is a godsend. Adding your Stamina, which you can blood buff if needed, to your soak against Aggravated (except for fire, magic and sunlight), and reducing the difficulty of all soak by 1, is amazing. Serpentis 3 on its own is like getting several ranks of RAW Fortitude, just with some terms and conditions. If you're an Apostate and you do in fact have Fortitude, all the better, since they synergize well. Serpentis 3 with high Stamina and a few ranks of Fortitude is very achievable EXP wise and provides a lot of protection.<br /> <br /> 4: Snake Form is kind of weird. It takes multiple turns to assume and the main benefit seems to be becoming a snake. I'm reminded of the Evil Overlord Advice list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>34. I will not turn into a snake. It never helps.</b> </div> </div> </div>5: Heart removal is a handy power, but it feels more like a Setite Sorcery ritual than anything else. Useful, but thematically weird for a Discipline which up until now has been snaky powers.<br /> <br /> I would suggest making heart removal a 5th level Akhu ritual, and replacing Serpentis 5 with another suitable power. Mother of Monsters from DAV20 is an interesting replacement, although it does feel like a weird jump in the abilities of the Discipline. So far we've been transforming our own bodies... giving birth to monsters feels like yet another power which is a high level blood magic effect.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, Serpentis is a potent, fun and thematically exciting Discipline which will spice up any party. The main problems are 4 (somewhat lackluster, the main advantage is turning into an enormous snake, something that will not blend in most of the world over, and the benefits it gives are already provided by other powers) and 5 (requires replacement).<br /> <br /> Ultimately I believe that the Discipline is perfect as is if you only seek to take levels 1-3, which is a great place for a Discipline to be, leaving you plenty of EXP to spend on other pursuits. 4 is mostly fun for having the ability to turn into a huge snake, which is its own reward. 5 should be turning into a swarm of snakes or something else sufficiently serpentine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T06:18:01-07:00","id":1452316,"title":"","content":"Thematically and in terms of getting a balance of utility right, it's probably my second favorite of the &quot;Protean knockoff clan disciplines&quot;. But that's the problem with it: until DAV20, it was a &quot;Protean knockoff clan discipline&quot; and writers/publishers never pushed away from that mold to give the discipline its own identity that it deserves. I've never had an issue with Serpentis taking the &quot;Conan the Barbarian bad guy&quot; theme rather than preserving fidelity with Egyptian myth, but given DAV20 manages to break that mold without sacrificing utility I'm strongly in favor of DAV20 Serpentis over practically any past version of it.<br /> <br /> My only issue with DAV20 Serpentis is they wrote it in the mold of DAV20 Vicissitude, where level 5 is &quot;disposable minion creation power&quot; opposed to &quot;immunity/survival power&quot;.<br /> <br /> But honestly, level 1 is the most powerful level of Serpentis. Effectively hard countering every social discipline in the game is a hell of a power, especially for what a smart player can do in combination with practically any level of Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 06-15-2021, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T07:05:29-07:00","id":1452320,"title":"","content":"Serpentis was always meant to be a Protean knockoff. Protean is actually meant to be a big, diverse, messy and interesting discipline, like thaumaturgy (but also the opposite of thaumaturgy because that one's about the soul and this one's about the Beast) Serpentis is just Protean through a lense of faith (but the Settites will not look kindly on anyone spouting such heretical slander). Thanatosis and Visceraticka are also Protean. Most thinbloods thinking they're inceptors are just using Protean. The word literally means &quot;frequently and fast changing&quot;; it's only standardized because the beast is lazy and won't go the extra mile unless you push it too, and most vampires outside of the natural protean clans don't have that much of a reason to really delve that far into the discipline when the most broadly useful powers are the default five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T07:30:23-07:00","id":1452324,"title":"","content":"Indeed, the Tlacique make this very obvious, since they don't even have Serpentis, but use Protean instead. It's a bit lazy, and an approach the developers took more than once (I'm looking at you, Visceratika). It's simply that Protean is very well designed, it does what it's supposed to do, and has great utility, so why not copy it? If it ain't broke, etc.. Serpentis is really good in it's current form, although level 4 could use a buff (I simply give it the same stat points that Revised Gangrel get for their animal forms in their Clanbook, giving players the option of a small venomous snake or a larger constrictor). 5 has always been goofy, and the Tlacique solve this by making it an actual Ritual. I rather liked the DAV20 version just because it's unique, if a bit strong.<br /> <br /> The weird part of Serpentis is it's always lacked a central theme. It doesn't even really make you all that snake-like (last I checked, snakes don't have feeding tongues), and the higher levels start stealing the powers of other Disciplines to reflect this. Seriously, there's one higher level Serpentis power that is basically Obtenebration (something Set should have anyways, being a &quot;God of Darkness&quot;). It's as if they said &quot;Well, they should really have Obtenebration, Protean, and Sorcery, but that's way too good&quot;. Then, satisfied with a half-baked job well done, they went ahead and created the original Samedi and Kiasyd...lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T09:17:16-07:00","id":1452337,"title":"","content":"I feel DAV20 also does it a diservice. The good they did was change the 5th power into a Thaumaturgy ritual and replace it with something more like mist form. The bad they did with it was plenty; 2 is REALLY FUCKING POWERFUL. 4 is too magical, and 3 is... I forgot what they did for 3. DAV20 also did this shift towards disciplines being more customizable, like you could choose the visuals for how fortitude worked; arrows can bounce off your skin or you can get visually F'd up beyond recognition and still act like you're healthy. . Protean and Serpentis were super personalizable... which, sounds cool to a layman, but it gives off the connotation that the state of vampirism cares for your whims. <br /> DAV20 is like, the best and worst of onyx path really. All those freelancers with different skills and ideas and a light-handed editor make for a really mixed bag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T09:33:24-07:00","id":1452339,"title":"","content":"My take on how I'd rebalance the Discipline:<br /> <br /> 1: DAV20 version<br /> <br /> 2: V20 version<br /> <br /> 3: DAV20 version<br /> <br /> 4: Upgrade the V20 version of level 2 to the DAV20 version, since the DAV20 version of 2 is very powerful<br /> <br /> 5: Transform into either a large snake the size of yourself or a swarm of tiny snakes which can crawl over and through most things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T16:54:09-07:00","id":1452392,"title":"","content":"Serpentis originally had two mummy-flavored powers, Mummify at level three and Heart of Darkness at level five. When the three-dot power was thrown out in Revised but the five-dot power was left untouched, the end result was that the latter now looked out of place among otherwise snake-themed powers.<br /> <br /> The original version of Serpentis was written at a time when Thaumaturgical rituals were not the answer to everything. In 1991, Thaumaturgy was still a relatively small set of powers, and primarily within the purview of the Tremere clan. The suggestion that Heart of Darkness &quot;should&quot; have been a ritual makes little sense in the original context.<br /> <br /> I feel like the criticism also mistakes the flavor text for the actual power. Cutting out your own heart is just how the Heart of Darkness is flavored; the actual power is &quot;You become immune to staking.&quot; I can think of a dozen ways to rewrite the description without making it seem like a one-time ritual. Compare the power to the original six-dot Daimonion power, which makes the Baali immune to fire. I've never heard anyone suggest that Ignore the Searing Flames should have also been a ritual, because it's not written to seem like one. Both the Serpentis and Daimonion powers are simply meant to give the user a blanket immunity to a common vampire weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":".  Corrected the publication date of the original Players Guide 06-16-2021, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T17:08:42-07:00","id":1452393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452324#post1452324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird part of Serpentis is it's always lacked a central theme. It doesn't even really make you all that snake-like (last I checked, snakes don't have feeding tongues), and the higher levels start stealing the powers of other Disciplines to reflect this. Seriously, there's one higher level Serpentis power that is basically Obtenebration (something Set should have anyways, being a &quot;God of Darkness&quot;). It's as if they said &quot;Well, they should really have Obtenebration, Protean, and Sorcery, but that's way too good&quot;. Then, satisfied with a half-baked job well done, they went ahead and created the original Samedi and Kiasyd...lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of this really makes any sense. Serpentis always had a central theme that was clearly stated in the original 1991 writeup: &quot;Most of the powers work around the concept of corruption in one way or another.&quot; It's really the level 1-5 powers that are the oddballs -- the original level 6-10 powers are all clearly centered around spiritual corruption. The higher level powers also don't duplicate any other discipline. Obtenebration <i>was not even written</i> at the time when Serpentis was created. The one high-level power that is &quot;basically Obtenebration&quot; (Shadow of Apep) was added only a decade later in the Revised Followers of Set clanbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":".  Corrected the publication date of the original Players Guide 06-16-2021, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T19:03:36-07:00","id":1452409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452392#post1452392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serpentis originally had two mummy-flavored powers, Mummify at level three and Heart of Darkness at level five. When the three-dot power was thrown out in Revised but the five-dot power was left untouched, the end result was that the latter now looked out of place among otherwise snake-themed powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Original Serpentis was like two different Disciplines merged into one. The first was &quot;Robert E. Howard style Stygian snake magic&quot; and the second was &quot;Egyptian Afterlife/Mummy magic&quot;. It only makes sense when you realize the intent was to create one power set that would give the Setites all the signature powers that you might expect from Ancient Egyptian snake worshipping cultists. Like you said in the next post, once they accomplished that they actually spent effort making the higher Discipline examples with a theme of &quot;corruption&quot; (which by nature were mainly an NPC thing as no PC could learn those Disciplines with any generation bought at character creation).<br /> <br /> So it never made too much sense from an in character or setting perspective as a combination of Egyptian funeral magic and snake transformation don't make sense outside of Howard's stories. It was for meta-narrative purposes to emulate a specific kind of pulp villain. As the setting began to distance itself from direct inspiration from Robert E. Howard in Revised, it undermined the very theme of Serpentis since the clan was no longer about emulating Howard's pulp villains. Simply put the Discipline is an artifact of the original &quot;Earth-One&quot; version of the WoD that doesn't make sense in the post-Revised setting but out of a sense of continuity it remains.<br /> <br /> This is why people now want to interpret either as an offshoot of Protean (it's just about shapechanging!), Blood Magic (it's obviously some kind of magical rituals!), or Obtenebration (Set is a God of Darkness!) because they want it to make sense in the setting. I don't think that's a wrong approach necessarily, but whatever style you choose, it is just a matter of taste. Just like if you want to be solely about corruption, or return it just to being Howard's cult of Stygian sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Personally I love REH's work and don't mind it being in the game. So I keep it like Stygian sorcerer, and just make the classic Serpentis a unique brand of Blood Magic. And I then have that and a few other Thaumaturgical Paths be proprietary to the Setites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T00:57:47-07:00","id":1452429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452409#post1452409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. Original Serpentis was like two different Disciplines merged into one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no insight into the writing process of the original <i>Players Guide,</i> but I have to wonder if at some point during development Serpentis looked very different from the finished product. It's funny that the same book that has the higher levels of Serpentis revolve around spiritual corruption and physical disfiguration <i>also</i> introduces the Thaumaturgical path of Corruption, a set of lower level powers all about spiritual corruption and physical disfiguration. Although the book assures the reader that Corruption is &quot;a natural one for the Tremere&quot;, to me it almost seems like a thematically coherent ten-level discipline got ripped apart at some point, levels 1-5 were handed to the Tremere, and levels 6-10 were given to the Setites:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Contradict<br /> \u2022\u2022 Disfiguration<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Change Mind<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Cripple<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Corrupt Soul<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 Obsession<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 Temptation<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022 Phobia<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022 Corruption<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Form of Corruption<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Mark of Damnation<br /> <br /> I don't know. Whatever the case, I don't think this hypothetical &quot;proto-Serpentis&quot; would make for a very <i>fun</i> discipline to use. The published version may be a grab-bag of disparate ideas, but I think the OP is right on the money when they say that low levels of Serpentis are just really cool and fun. Certainly moreso than going around disfiguring people or changing their Natures and Demeanors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T01:18:23-07:00","id":1452430,"title":"","content":"[Redacted] (Not sure what possessed me to write that) ...but going back to the origins of the clan is kinda like going back to the days were Assamites were &quot;Muslamic&quot; demons or ravnos were &quot;Gypsies&quot;. Egyptian wyrm cults just seem a bit racist without any of the later nuance attached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-17-2021, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T01:45:31-07:00","id":1452431,"title":"","content":"Was someone attacking you personally? I don't see it.<br /> <br /> I'm in my thirties, I was seven years old when <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> first came out, I never even read any World of Darkness products until after 2004, and I certainly didn't play or run <i>Vampire</i> until the original World of Darkness product line was already discontinued. Just like it's possible to listen to music or watch movies released before one's adulthood, it's entirely possible for a person interested in the history of a game to go back and read the original releases to see various concepts in their original context.<br /> <br /> My entire World of Darkness library is also digital, including my PDF copy of the 1991 <i>Players Guide</i> bought from DriveThruRPG a few years back. But thanks for the ageist potshot, I guess? You missed your mark by a long shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T03:06:41-07:00","id":1452435,"title":"","content":"Point being, bringing up the OG settites is silly, because efforts have gone in to erasing the OG settites, who should be seen as little more than a growing pain, and replacing them with an actual workable cult.<br /> Glory to Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T05:52:07-07:00","id":1452455,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the opinion piece, but I think the rest of us are fine without attempts to police the conversation. I've never understood the extremely online phenomenon where people have to loudly state their opinions about subject matters that they by their own admission are not even familiar with.<br /> <br /> If the conversation is about how strange the latest iteration of a given discipline appears to someone unfamiliar with the history behind it, putting things in context is not a claim about the superiority of the earliest version compared to later ones. My approach to game design is that if you want to understand why a recent edition of a game does something unexpected, <i>of course</i> you should go back to the earliest possible versions of the rules to see them in their original context and to get a sense of how and why the rules have changed in the hands of new designers. Otherwise you're just inheriting assumptions, concepts, and unnecessary cruft without even realizing it, which is exactly how we ended up with both 20th Anniversary versions of Serpentis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:01:26-07:00","id":1452456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452393#post1452393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of this really makes any sense. Serpentis always had a central theme that was clearly stated in the original 1991 writeup: &quot;Most of the powers work around the concept of corruption in one way or another.&quot; It's really the level 1-5 powers that are the oddballs -- the original level 6-10 powers are all clearly centered around spiritual corruption. The higher level powers also don't duplicate any other discipline. Obtenebration <i>was not even written</i> at the time when Serpentis was created. The one high-level power that is &quot;basically Obtenebration&quot; (Shadow of Apep) was added only a decade later in the Revised Followers of Set clanbook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm a little confused. You say that Serpentis has a central theme, but then point out that the 1-5 powers, the ones that are mostly used and seen in any game, make no sense. To me, that just reinforces my statement that Serpentis LACKS a central theme. It would be like if Presence was the power to manipulate emotions, but the 1-5 abilities made you better at shooting stuff because &quot;John Woo/The Matrix/John Wick is cool&quot;. Not trying to start a fight here, just hoping you see my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:21:58-07:00","id":1452460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452392#post1452392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Cutting out your own heart is just how the Heart of Darkness is flavored; the actual power is &quot;You become immune to staking&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly where concept doesn't match execution, perception doesn't meet reality, and player expectation doesn't line up with outcome.<br /> <br /> Staking...isn't really a big deal in the big picture. Were it a viable alternative to knocking a vampire into torpor through raw damage, or simply killing them, it would be a bigger deal but it isn't. Staking an active vampire is prohibitively difficult, and staking a debilitated or sleeping vampire is easier but the cost-to-benefit ratio is out of whack. Either an aggressor was capable of debilitating a vampire, thus in all likelihood they were capable of <i>killing</i> it, or they did the legwork of tracking a vampire's haven down and <i>still</i> being able to just kill it.<br /> <br /> In any case, staking is only an ideal resolution to a given problem, in such a small sliver of generally plot-related circumstances, it's frankly hardly worth the thought. Realistically, a storyteller needs to build a story from the ground up, with the specific intent of a vampire ending up staked (or getting un-staked), for it to even measure on the radar of dramatic events which might happen during a given chronicle.<br /> <br /> That's not a great basis for a capstone discipline power.<br /> <br /> Least of all when other disciplines -- namely, Vicissitude -- provide an analogous (I'd argue, superior) benefit to the possessor at level 1. To others, level 2. And a more powerful benefit overall that doesn't impart a pivotal weakness to the character, level 3. And that's available to all regardless whether they have Vicissitude or have a friendly local Tzimisce to do it, care of a two-point merit. Because the heart's still in the vampire and therefore doesn't require additional resources to protect, and in the case of Vicissitude, it can be up-armored.<br /> <br /> This is where the Robert E. Howard, &quot;Setites were originally written to be designated bad guys for PC's to eventually hunt/kill&quot;, shit rears its ugly head again. The discipline was purpose-built to give Setites a targetable Achilles' heel for a coterie of PC vampires to exploit, as you'd expect of any overblown, melodramatic, pulp fiction-inspired BBEG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 06-16-2021, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T10:57:43-07:00","id":1452506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452456#post1452456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused. You say that Serpentis has a central theme, but then point out that the 1-5 powers, the ones that are mostly used and seen in any game, make no sense. To me, that just reinforces my statement that Serpentis LACKS a central theme. It would be like if Presence was the power to manipulate emotions, but the 1-5 abilities made you better at shooting stuff because &quot;John Woo/The Matrix/John Wick is cool&quot;. Not trying to start a fight here, just hoping you see my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your other statements -- that the clan should have had Obtenebration from the beginning, and that the higher levels of Serpentis are stolen from other disciplines -- that I was also reacting to. The claims make little sense in the original context. I don't disagree with you that Serpentis was always a grab-bag of various ideas that don't form a coherent whole, and I even speculated idly on why that might have been. I would only phrase the criticism a little differently:<br /> <br /> We have the designers' own words about what the discipline was originally meant to represent -- &quot;the concept of corruption in one way or another.&quot; It's not that Serpentis lacks a central theme, it's that only the Elder level powers successfully capture that theme. I don't know the thinking process behind the original design, but if I had to wager a guess, the designers probably viewed the snake-themed powers as manifestations of, or vehicles for, physical corruption. Beginners learn to corrupt the vampiric body in a very tangible manner, and only at higher levels do Serpentis users work toward the subtler, more spiritual corruption that used to be the <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i> of the clan.<br /> <br /> A modern rewrite of the discipline could probably tease out the original intent and sharpen it up so the discipline wouldn't seem so incoherent. Such a rewrite would certainly be a more sophisticated effort than just giving Setites Protean and calling it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T11:51:17-07:00","id":1452513,"title":"","content":"This is why I think combining all the Disciplines into a core ten and allowing players to choose from multiple powers per level was such a good idea of V5's. It never made sense for earlier editions to restrict multiple powers per level to 6+ levels only. Granted, it didn't make sense either for V5 to say &quot;you can choose from multiple powers per level, but you can't take more than one&quot; either, but that's easily ig<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">nored.</span></span><br /> <br /> Serpentis works fine as Protean powers for the physical shapeshifting and Presence powers (or Blood Sorcery) for the spiritual corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T12:10:17-07:00","id":1452516,"title":"","content":"The big draw for Serpentis 5 seemed to be that you can take out the hearts of OTHER people and use them as hostages. <br /> But that's very... not Protean. Protean is too personal and too temporary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T12:24:06-07:00","id":1452518,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider when talking about the original design of the Setites and Serpentis, is that the Setites were closely tied to them being servants and priests of the Wyrm. The Wyrm being one of those things that served to tie the various game lines together as part of a common metaphysics of the setting, but most closely associated with Werewolf. This usually is not stated directly in Vampire sourcebooks, but is quickly gleaned from other material where the Setites are mentioned.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm being both a source of corruption and associated with serpents, lends itself to most of the original powers of Serpentis. It could be looked at as &quot;how to be a servant to the Wyrm&quot;.<br /> <br /> In this scenario, the hodgepodge powers make better sense thematically although it seems best emulated as a kind of unique path of Dark Thaumaturgy than its own Discipline. But even that can be overlooked if we assume the Wyrm was somehow involved in the creation of vampires (and even reconciled with Vampire's Noddist mythology if we just call it the Serpent of Eden) and therefore Serpentis as &quot;inherent&quot; and not sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T13:14:14-07:00","id":1452524,"title":"","content":"I'm certainly a big fan of the OG Followers of Set as priests of the Wyrm! I just think it's neat how the Garou, Setites, Mummies, and even tiny oddball factions like the Children of Osiris were all intimately tied together in the deep background of the World of Darkness. That sort of crossover-palooza is very much out of fashion these days, but it made for a very vibrant setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T13:54:14-07:00","id":1452529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452324#post1452324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, the Tlacique make this very obvious, since they don't even have Serpentis, but use Protean instead. It's a bit lazy, and an approach the developers took more than once (I'm looking at you, Visceratika). It's simply that Protean is very well designed, it does what it's supposed to do, and has great utility, so why not copy it? If it ain't broke, etc.. Serpentis is really good in it's current form, although level 4 could use a buff (I simply give it the same stat points that Revised Gangrel get for their animal forms in their Clanbook, giving players the option of a small venomous snake or a larger constrictor). 5 has always been goofy, and the Tlacique solve this by making it an actual Ritual. I rather liked the DAV20 version just because it's unique, if a bit strong.<br /> <br /> The weird part of Serpentis is it's always lacked a central theme. It doesn't even really make you all that snake-like (last I checked, snakes don't have feeding tongues), and the higher levels start stealing the powers of other Disciplines to reflect this. Seriously, there's one higher level Serpentis power that is basically Obtenebration (something Set should have anyways, being a &quot;God of Darkness&quot;). It's as if they said &quot;Well, they should really have Obtenebration, Protean, and Sorcery, but that's way too good&quot;. Then, satisfied with a half-baked job well done, they went ahead and created the original Samedi and Kiasyd...lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>There appears to be an in-universe reason for this. When we started assembling the various pieces of WoD historical lore from the editions for the &quot;<i>Set and Osiris</i>&quot; thread, they formed a very coherent story:<br /> <br /> Set was originally embraced as a Gangrel by Ennoia (His oldest bloodline has Protean rather than Serpentis, he has animal features, is childer get animal features, he was embraced long after the killing of the Second Generation, and a number of other issues). Set diablerized the Antediluvian Typhon, an obtenebration-user to get to the Third Generation. Typhon took him over or is taking him over. (Set was originally a storm and warrior god, the myths about Typhon has him killed by a redheaded storm god. Set had a big personality change not long after, went from a storm and warrior god to the the snakes and corruption theme, changed his name to Typhon Set, his clan got exterminated and restarted, he wiped out all records from before that, he named his philosophy and his pet after Typhon, etc.)<br /> <br /> So you originally had this Gangrel who diablerized his way to the 3rd. He redeveloped Protean into Serpentis, and during the process the original Antediluvian influences/takes him over. Typhon was the one with the snakes and corruption motif, not originally Set. So the shifts in focus for the discipline makes a lot of sense given its in-universe history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T14:46:14-07:00","id":1452541,"title":"","content":"Oh is Typhon the founder of the Ramanga, then? Well Serpentis having a power that mimics Obtenebration makes a little more sense now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T15:50:48-07:00","id":1452550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452541#post1452541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh is Typhon the founder of the Ramanga, then? Well Serpentis having a power that mimics Obtenebration makes a little more sense now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not be surprised at all if he was. He was going around Africa, or at least the parts of it close to the Second City, and embracing rulers to use their forces for his own purposes. He embraced Osiris, and it would be an established pattern for him to have more childer in Africa.<br /> <br /> The name Typhon is what he named himself to Osiris court. It is from an Indo-European root meaning &quot;<i>Abyss</i>&quot; or &quot;<i>serpent of the deep</i>&quot; The language was just expanding from the pontic-Caspian steppes, so when he introduced himself as &quot;<i>I am Typhon&quot;</i> he would actually be saying &quot;<i>I am Abyss</i>&quot; He also seems to have been called Apep and Brujah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T03:26:39-07:00","id":1452603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452308-revisiting-disciplines-serpentis-1-3-is-really-great?p=1452430#post1452430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, because, y'know, I'm not 40, and thus obscure 1st edition supplements aren't something I have on the shelf (I don't have anything WoD on my shelf, it's ALL PDFS, wrap that around your elderly heads) So basically everything I've read is from the phase where everything in Serpentis was either -Protean- or -Thaumaturgy even though the settites clearly have access to Akhu so I don't see why....<br /> <br /> Every time someone gets out the &quot;Ha they were originally pulp snake people who sacrifice hot virgins in provocative poses so that Conan/Flash Gordon/Donald Duck/Popeye could rescue them&quot; I just get confused. The current power set is still good for mustache twirling, but going back to the origins of the clan is kinda like going back to the days were Assamites were &quot;Muslamic&quot; demons or ravnos were &quot;Gypsies&quot;;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Making fun of gamers age is a weird stance to call, especially when you are a die-hard warrior for a previous edition. Eventually, barring undeath, we all reach an older age too.<br /> <br /> Please leave the thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}